  "rules": [
    "Do not delete a legacy root before file-level classification.",
    "Do not copy content merely to create bilingual symmetry.",
    "Do not assign artifact identity from physical path alone.",
    "Do not mark a family physically consolidated until references and tests pass.",
    "Preserve historical provenance for migrated artifacts.",
    "A consolidated family has one canonical owner even while legacy aliases remain temporarily resolvable.",
    "For duplicate PT/EN families, classify every legacy artifact, merge complementary content into the canonical owner, then validate consumers before physical removal.",
    "The ELO must maintain logical coherence inside each canonical family: every artifact needs a clear purpose, place in the flow, owner, consumers and relationship to adjacent artifacts.",
    "When a duplicate family is processed, the ELO must repeat the same file-level semantic audit until no useful, non-incongruent legacy content remains outside the canonical owner."
